* GITUDIFF - the engine op, as a SUBROUTINE.  See BP/GITSTATUS.
*
* NO REPO PARAMETER, unlike every other op here: a unified diff is computed from
* two CONTENTS and never opens a repository.  The C side always ignored the one
* it was given (it was copied from the UniData CallC entry point, which carries
* repo for symmetry), and the extra parameter made this shim disagree with the
* shared CALL in GIT.OBJ -- SUBROUTINE_PARM_ERROR the moment jBASE started
* taking the engine branch (mv_git#183).
      SUBROUTINE GITUDIFF(OLDTEXT, NEWTEXT, PATH, ANS)
      DEFC VAR JBGITUDIFF(VAR, VAR, VAR, VAR)
      ANS = ""
      X = JBGITUDIFF(OLDTEXT, NEWTEXT, PATH, ANS)
      RETURN
